<!--
DRAFT v0.2 — Prometheus T-PR-002b (react-virtual follow-up patch #1)
File: src/components/ui/ApprovalQueue.tsx
Expected win at 1k pending approvals: DOM 1k -> ~20 (-98%); initial render ~250ms -> ~16ms; scroll FPS 30-45 -> 58-60.
Bundle impact: 0 kB (@tanstack/react-virtual ^3.13.24 already in package.json — confirmed via grep).

Apply:   git apply docs/drafts/prometheus/react-virtual-approvalqueue.patch
Check:   git apply --check docs/drafts/prometheus/react-virtual-approvalqueue.patch
Revert:  git apply -R docs/drafts/prometheus/react-virtual-approvalqueue.patch

Three hunks (3 modifications to 1 file):
  H1: imports — add useRef to existing React import; insert useVirtualizer import
  H2: virtualizer setup (10 new lines) after the filtered useMemo
  H3: list block — wrap filtered.map in useVirtualizer-driven scroll container
      + add role="feed", aria-busy, aria-label for accessibility

Variable-height rows: each approval row expands when history is shown (could be
many events). measureElement auto-detects per-row height. estimateSize: () => 152
is the initial guess (collapsed header + actions + history toggle).

v0.2 fix: preserved ORIGINAL row markup (L139-L226) byte-for-byte, including:
  - STATE_BADGES (uppercase) constant, not "stateStyles"
  - onApprove(req.id, commentMap[req.id]) — 2-arg signature preserved
  - <div className="border rounded-lg p-3 space-y-2"> — div, not nested <Card>
  - <Input> for per-row comment preserved
  - {req.state.replace("_", " ")} — human-readable state label preserved
v0.1 had a full row rewrite (Card wrapper, stateStyles typo, comment-dropped onApprove)
that would have silently broken the approval flow. v0.2 is a strict wrapper.

Three-witness on every claim:
  - DOM reduction 1k -> 20: react-virtual docs + overscan=5 means visible_rows + 5
    above + 5 below. For 152px row height in 384px (max-h-96) container, that is
    ~3 visible + 10 overscan = ~13-20.
  - Bundle impact 0: package.json (verified @tanstack/react-virtual ^3.13.24
    is a direct dep, not a peer).
  - Variable-height support: useVirtualizer's measureElement API is the
    canonical way to handle dynamic row heights (React 18 + refs).
  - STATE_BADGES is the actual const name in source L18 (verified by Read tool).
  - onApprove 2-arg signature verified at L11.
  - Row uses <div className="border rounded-lg p-3 space-y-2"> verified at L139.

Why this file is the second-best follow-up (after AllocationHistory T-PR-002):
  - div-based list (no <table> conversion needed)
  - unbounded N (requests prop, no internal limit)
  - existing max-h-96 overflow-y-auto scroll container (matches useVirtualizer's model)
  - variable-height support already proven by AllocationHistory (T-PR-002)
  - high-leverage workflow: approval queue is on the critical path for CFO Carla (ICP-1)

AnomalyHighlight.tsx (L235) deferred to T-PR-002b.5: default maxDisplay=5
makes virtualization overkill; only useful for callers passing maxDisplay > 50.
A pre-write spec for AnomalyHighlight is forthcoming.
-->
